## What It Is
Dodo is a graphical, hackable email client built in Python/PyQt6. It provides a
vim-like, keyboard-driven interface on top of the [notmuch](https://notmuchmail.org/)
email indexer.

## Core Philosophy
- Keyboard-oriented with keychord support (e.g. `g g` for top, `t m` to tag marked)
- UNIX philosophy: offloads work to battle-tested CLI tools (notmuch, mbsync, msmtp, w3m)
- Text-first by default; HTML view is one keystroke away (`H`)
- Fully configurable via `~/.config/dodo/config.py` (exec'd Python)
- Non-destructive: all operations go through notmuch tags; no email is lost

## Architecture

### Layout (Split-Pane UX)
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ MainWindow (QSplitter)                                  │
│ ┌───────────────────────┐ ┌───────────────────────────┐ │
│ │ QTabWidget (list)     │ │ Thread Preview (persistent)│ │
│ │ ┌───────────────────┐ │ │                           │ │
│ │ │ DashboardPanel    │ │ │ ThreadPanel               │ │
│ │ │ SearchPanel       │ │ │ (message list + viewer)   │ │
│ │ │ ComposePanel      │ │ │                           │ │
│ │ │ TagPanel          │ │ │                           │ │
│ │ └───────────────────┘ │ │                           │ │
│ └───────────────────────┘ └───────────────────────────┘ │
│ CommandBar / StatusBar                                   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```
- Thread preview is always visible (configurable: right/left/below/above)
- `Enter` on a thread → swaps preview content in-place; no thread tabs
- `Escape` in preview → focus back to list
- `h`/`l` navigate list tabs only
- `j`/`k` in list: navigate threads; `J`/`K` in thread: navigate messages

### Class Hierarchy
```
QApplication
 └── Dodo (app.py) — global commands, sync, status bar messages

QMainWindow
 └── MainWindow (mainwindow.py)
      ├── QTabWidget (tabs)
      │    └── Panel (panel.py) — base class
      │         ├── DashboardPanel (dashboard.py) — multi-query inbox dashboard
      │         ├── SearchPanel (search.py) — notmuch query results
      │         ├── ThreadPanel (thread.py) — single thread + message viewer
      │         ├── ComposePanel (compose.py) — compose/reply/forward
      │         └── TagPanel (tag.py) — tag browser
      ├── CommandBar (commandbar.py) — search/tag input with autocomplete
      ├── StatusBar (status_label) — transient messages (sync progress, errors)
      └── HelpWindow (helpwindow.py) — three-column keybinding reference
```

### Module Map
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `app.py` | `Dodo(QApplication)`, `SyncMailThread` (with live progress signal), `main()` |
| `mainwindow.py` | `MainWindow`: split-pane layout (tabs + persistent thread preview), command bar, status bar |
| `panel.py` | `Panel(QWidget)`: keychord handling, dirty tracking, temp dir cleanup |
| `dashboard.py` | `DashboardPanel` + `DashboardModel`: multi-section inbox view |
| `search.py` | `SearchPanel` + `SearchModel` + `render_thread_cell()`: thread listing with `#` count column |
| `thread.py` | `ThreadPanel`: message viewer, reply/forward, attachments |
| `thread_model.py` | `ThreadModel` + `ThreadItem` + helpers: thread-tree data model (extracted from thread.py) |
| `webengine.py` | `MessagePage` + `MessageHandler` + `EmbeddedImageHandler` + `RemoteBlockingUrlRequestInterceptor` (extracted from thread.py) |
| `actions.py` | `move_to_trash()`, `move_to_archive()`, `check_archive_refused()`: shared delete/archive logic |
| `compose.py` | `ComposePanel` + `EditorThread` + `SendmailThread` |
| `tag.py` | `TagPanel` + `TagModel`: tag browser with counts |
| `commandbar.py` | `CommandBar(QLineEdit)`: tag autocomplete + command history |
| `keymap.py` | All keymaps (global, dashboard, search, thread, compose, tag, command_bar) |
| `settings.py` | Config defaults incl. `mail_root`, `dashboard_queries`, `dashboard_max_items` |
| `themes.py` | Theme dicts + `apply_theme()` |
| `util.py` | HTML/text helpers, case-insensitive email matching, key parsing |
| `helpwindow.py` | `HelpWindow`: three-column keybinding layout |
| `pgp_util.py` | PGP/MIME signing and encryption |

### Data Flow
1. **Search**: `notmuch search --format=json` → `SearchModel` → `QTreeView` (5 cols: date, #, from, subject, tags)
2. **Dashboard**: multiple `SearchModel` instances → `DashboardModel` (flat model with section headers) → single QTreeView
3. **Thread**: `notmuch show --format=json --include-html` → `ThreadModel` → message list + QWebEngineView (via custom URL scheme `message:`)
4. **Compose**: raw email string → external editor → `SendmailThread` pipes to msmtp → saved to Maildir sent folder
5. **Sync**: `SyncMailThread` runs `mbsync -a -V`, streams output to status bar via `progress` signal, then `notmuch new`
6. **Delete**: `d` → `+deleted` tag + move file to Trash folder (Thunderbird/neomutt approach) — centralized in `actions.py`
7. **Archive-to-local**: `A` → `-inbox -unread` + move file to local Archive Maildir — centralized in `actions.py`

### Sync Flow (Ruly's Setup)
- `mbsync -a -V`: syncs Gmail (`RulyTafzil@gmail.com/`) and contact (`contact@RulyTafzil.com/`)
- `notmuch new`: indexes new mail, applies `unread;inbox;` tags
- `post-new` hook: maps Maildir folders → notmuch tags, strips inbox/unread from Trash
- `synchronize_flags=true`: D/F/P/R/S flag sync (not T — deletion uses folder move instead)

## Key Bindings

### Global
| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `?` | Help (three-column layout) |
| `D` | Open/re-focus dashboard |
| `/` | Search bar |
| `t t` | Tag current thread |
| `t m` | Tag all marked threads |
| `` ` `` | Manual sync |
| `Q` | Quit |
| `h/l` | Previous/next tab |
| `x/X` | Close panel / close all |
| `c` | Compose |
| `I/U/F/T` | Show inbox / unread / flagged / tags |

### Dashboard & Search
| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `j/k` | Next/previous thread (auto-opens in preview) |
| `<enter>` | Open/focus thread preview |
| `a` | Archive (refuses if no categorizing tag) |
| `d` | Delete (move to Trash folder) |
| `u/f` | Toggle unread/flagged |
| `<space>` | Toggle marked + advance |
| `g g/G` | First/last |
| `C-d/C-u` | Page down/up |

### Thread View
| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `J/K` or `<enter>` | Next/previous message |
| `j/k` | Scroll down/up |
| `<escape>` | Focus back to list |
| `<space>` / `-` | Page down/up |
| `H` | Toggle HTML/plaintext |
| `r/R` | Reply / reply all |
| `C-f` | Forward |
| `d` | Delete current message |
| `A` | Open attachments |

### Compose
| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `<enter>` | Edit in external editor |
| `S` | Send |
| `a` | Attach file |
| `[/]` | Cycle SMTP accounts |
| `s/e` | Toggle PGP sign/encrypt |

## Custom Features (Deviations from Upstream)

### Dashboard Panel
- Multi-section inbox view: queries configured via `dashboard_queries` setting
- Section headers span all columns, non-selectable
- Unified scroll with j/k navigation skipping headers
- Column widths persist via QSettings
- Auto-opens on startup (replaces `init_queries`)

### Status Bar
- `MainWindow.show_status(message, kind, duration)` — supported kinds: info/warning/error
- `duration=0` keeps message until replaced (used for sync progress)
- `Dodo.status_message()` convenience method callable from any panel
- Used for: sync progress, archive refusal, delete confirmations, errors

### Delete Workflow
- `d` moves files to Trash folder (matching Thunderbird/neomutt)
- Strips mbsync UID annotations to avoid duplicate UID errors
- Trash folder auto-detected per account (`[Gmail]/Trash` or `Trash`)
- Post-new hook strips inbox/unread from Trash folder files
- Two-stage: soft-delete to Trash (recoverable), empty trash later for expunge
- Centralized in `dodo/actions.py` → `move_to_trash()`

### Archive-to-Local Workflow
- `A` moves files to local-only Archive Maildir (outside synced IMAP folders)
- Refuses threads without categorizing tags
- Centralized in `dodo/actions.py` → `move_to_archive()`

### Sync Progress
- `SyncMailThread.progress` signal emits per-mailbox status during sync
- Status bar shows real-time: "Syncing: gmail... INBOX Finances ..."
- Final summary parsed from mbsync output: "Sync: +3 new, 2 flagged"
- Uses `mbsync -a -V` (verbose) for detailed output

### Other Changes
- **Split-pane UX**: persistent thread preview (configurable via `thread_pane_position`)
- **Thread count column** (`#`): shows fa-comments icon + count for multi-message threads
- **Plaintext fallback**: HTML mode degrades to plaintext when no HTML part exists
- **Case-insensitive email matching**: `email_is_me` and `email_smtp_account_index`
- **Compose background fix**: no white flash when switching accounts
- **Three-column help window** layout
- **Column order**: `date | # | from | subject | tags`
- **Archive refuses** threads without categorizing tags (not just inbox/unread)
- `deleted`/`killed`/`spam` excluded from searches by default
- **`mail_root` setting**: configurable Maildir root (default `~/Mail`)
- **Shared rendering**: `render_thread_cell()` in search.py eliminates duplication between SearchModel and DashboardModel

### Refactoring (2025)
- **`dodo/actions.py`**: shared delete/archive/move logic extracted from 3 panels
- **`dodo/webengine.py`**: `MessagePage`, `MessageHandler`, `EmbeddedImageHandler`, `RemoteBlockingUrlRequestInterceptor` extracted from thread.py
- **`dodo/thread_model.py`**: `ThreadModel`, `ThreadItem`, `EmptyThreadError`, helpers extracted from thread.py
- **`render_thread_cell()`**: shared thread-row rendering in search.py, used by both SearchModel and DashboardModel
- Hardcoded `/home/rulyt/Mail/` paths replaced with `settings.mail_root`

